{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773086101,"nonce":"cAaI6qQt3aJ+OBzMjjMEtquqNq4=","title":"Service worker: new SW version waits for all tabs to close before activating","message":"With registerType: autoUpdate and no skipWaiting, when a new service worker is deployed, it waits until all existing instances (tabs/PWA windows) are closed before activating. This means deployed fixes (like the NetworkOnly graph cache fix) do not take effect until the user manually closes all instances.\n\nFix: add skipWaiting: true to the Workbox config in vite.config.ts so new service workers activate immediately on install.\n\nThis is especially important for a PWA that may stay open for long sessions.","files":null}]}